{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890188",
      "title": "Understanding Type Aliases",
      "sourceHash": "52b2592160f5df63b2d0875b064daf6affe28b5b578d5402d8589b39dc9f6b62",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 4.97,
          "en": "Now the more TypeScript code you're going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.97,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "write, the higher the chances that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "at some point you might be repeating some type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 15.08,
          "en": "And we're actually already doing this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.08,
          "end": 18.59,
          "en": "Here, for people, I'm saying that I want an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.59,
          "end": 20.88,
          "en": "of this kind of object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.88,
          "end": 22.21,
          "en": "So that I want an array full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.21,
          "end": 24.61,
          "en": "of objects that have this structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.61,
          "end": 26.87,
          "en": "And that's the same object I have up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.87,
          "end": 28.03,
          "en": "for person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.03,
          "end": 32.54,
          "en": "The same type definition just in the non array form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.54,
          "end": 35.29,
          "en": "But the object type is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.29,
          "end": 38.96,
          "en": "Now you can, of course, duplicate the type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.96,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "but it's more realistic that you wanna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 43.75,
          "en": "avoid that duplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.75,
          "end": 48.17,
          "en": "And for that, you can create a so-called type alias.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.17,
          "end": 51.52,
          "en": "You can define your own base type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.52,
          "end": 54.96,
          "en": "in which a more complex type definition is stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.96,
          "end": 58.31,
          "en": "and then use that type alias instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.31,
          "end": 61.273,
          "en": "of repeating the entire type definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.38,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "For that here, for example, before we use this object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 70.21000000000001,
          "en": "for the first time here, we can define such a type alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.21000000000001,
          "end": 72.35,
          "en": "with the type keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.35,
          "end": 74.27,
          "en": "And that's a keyword which does not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.27,
          "end": 76.97,
          "en": "exist in standard JavaScript but",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.97,
          "end": 79.283,
          "en": "which is added by TypeScript instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.568,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "Now, after this type keyword, you use any name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 88.73,
          "en": "of your choice which will be your new type name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.73,
          "end": 91.033,
          "en": "For example, person, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.15,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "And then after the equal sign here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 96.46000000000001,
          "en": "you then have a type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.46000000000001,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "because this is a pure TypeScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 102.38,
          "en": "This will basically be thrown out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.38,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "of the window when the code is compiled to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 108.43,
          "en": "So, here on the right side of the equal sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.43,
          "end": 113.14,
          "en": "it's not a JavaScript value, but instead a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.14,
          "end": 116.50999999999999,
          "en": "And that could be our object type definition here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.50999999999999,
          "end": 119.37,
          "en": "which I now store here in this person type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.37,
          "end": 123.62,
          "en": "And now in all those places where I used this object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.62,
          "end": 126.61,
          "en": "I can use my alias instead now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.61,
          "end": 128.66,
          "en": "And it's therefore still the same type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.66,
          "end": 130.58,
          "en": "but I only define it once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.58,
          "end": 134.75,
          "en": "And then I can repeat it in all the places where I need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.75,
          "end": 137.05,
          "en": "And I can still also change it like I'm doing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.05,
          "end": 141.28,
          "en": "down here to use it just as person like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.28,
          "end": 144.49,
          "en": "or to use it as an array full of persons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.49,
          "end": 146.393,
          "en": "That also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.64,
          "end": 151.4,
          "en": "And that's the very important feature of type aliases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.4,
          "end": 155.09,
          "en": "which can save you a lot of typing work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.09,
          "end": 158.55,
          "en": "and which can, therefore, make your code more concise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.55,
          "end": 160.433,
          "en": "and easier to maintain.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}